  S cut out of it, and the three bubbles off its shoulder.

  Paths are the source's own, in its 1024 coordinates. The group scales them by 2/3 about
  the centre, which is 72/108 — the factor that maps a square drawn to fill itself onto
  the part of an adaptive icon a launcher actually shows, so the droplet ends up the same
  fraction of the visible icon as it is of the source.

  The S is not drawn; it is the five bars removed from the droplet by `evenOdd`, which is
  the source's `fill-rule="evenodd"` and the whole trick of the mark.
-->
